</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl">I prostrate before the 
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl">sage Patanjali who has thousands of radiant, white heads (as the divine 
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl">serpent, Ananta) and who has, as far as his arms, assumed the form of a man holding a conch 
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl">shell (divine sound), a wheel (discus of light or infinite time) and a sword (discrimination
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl">) 
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl">OM</span></span></code></pre></div></div>
<div class="code-block code-line-numbers open" style="counter-reset: code-block 0">
