    </div><div class="highlight"><pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"><code class="language-fallback" data-lang="fallback"><span class="line"><span class="cl">OM
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl">Vande = bow 
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl">Gurunam = to the plurality of gurus 
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl">Caranaravinde = two lotus feet
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl">sandarsita = to bring to sight 
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl">Svatma = pure Being 
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl">Sukhava = happiness 
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl">Bodhe = awakened
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl">nishreyase = refuge 
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl">jangalikayamane = 
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl">jungle hut (meaning shaman, jungle physician)
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl">samsara = conditioned existence 
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl">halahala = poison 
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl">moha = delusion 
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl">santyai = peace
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl">abahu = down to the shoulders 
